{"ts": "2026-10-27T19:48:28.613934Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T1942Z-f5dd", "unit": "openspec:add-audit-chain", "seq": 80, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-002", "id": "Q-002", "status": "answered", "reason": "verify.ts lines 134-140 compare lastHash (the tip's hash) with head.hash whenever headSeq is between fromSeq and expected - 1, so a head below the tip is reported as a hash failure at headSeq. tasks.md task 5.2 says such a head passes, and design.md says appends during a verification are not tail loss. tx.ts opens the transaction with a bare BEGIN (read committed), so the head read and the walk are separate snapshots and a concurrent append produces exactly this state. The fix is in production code only.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "F-0447fea8", "kind": "verdict", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.056619, "decision": "reject", "answer_sha256": "8c7279bcf388381647c92326fdc1a0c41d3bdff945ba74494c99497cd559e344", "checked": [{"ref": "src/audit/verify.ts:134", "quote": "if (headSeq >= fromSeq) {\n        if (headSeq >= expected) {\n          return { ok: false, checked, firstBadSeq: expected, reason: \"gap\" };\n        }\n        if (lastHash === null || !lastHash.equals(head.hash)) {\n          return { ok: false, checked, firstBadSeq: headSeq, reason: \"hash\" };", "claim": "A head seq below the walked tip but at or above fromSeq is compared with the tip's hash and reported as a hash failure."}, {"ref": "src/audit/verify.ts:120", "quote": "lastHash = row.hash;", "claim": "lastHash is the hash of the last walked row, the tip, not the hash at the head's seq."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-audit-chain/tasks.md:22", "quote": "head `seq` above `tipSeq` gives `gap` at `tipSeq + 1n`; equal to `tipSeq` with a different `hash` gives `hash` at `tipSeq`; below `tipSeq`, or no head row, passes", "claim": "Task 5.2 requires a head below the tip to pass."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "The head is read before the walk, so appends during a verification are not tail loss", "claim": "The design expects a head that lags the walk because of concurrent appends to verify as intact."}, {"ref": "src/tenancy/tx.ts:40", "quote": "await client.query(\"BEGIN\");", "claim": "withTenantTx starts a plain read-committed transaction, so the head read and the walk can see different committed states."}]}
