{"ts": "2026-10-27T19:49:48.926829Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T1942Z-f5dd", "unit": "openspec:add-audit-chain", "seq": 90, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-004", "id": "Q-004", "status": "answered", "reason": "tasks.md 5.1 explicitly requires that canonicalEvent throwing yields reason hash. verify.ts lines 101-116 call chainHash without any try/catch and only compare the result; hash.ts canonicalEvent throws AUDIT_EVENT_INVALID bad_at when the at text fails AT_PATTERN, and canonicalize can throw AUDIT_CANONICAL_INVALID. So a throw propagates and verifyChain rejects instead of returning a hash report, contrary to the ticked task text. The fix is to production code only.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "F-1abb4766", "kind": "verdict", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.9173855000000001, "decision": "reject", "answer_sha256": "e90899f0f5cbada2635ed472d7cb0ff2539a937c39ae9ff6fc4af4791276b867", "checked": [{"ref": "openspec/changes/add-audit-chain/tasks.md:21", "quote": "`chainHash(prev, rec)` not equal to the stored `hash` (or `canonicalEvent` throwing) gives `hash`", "claim": "Task 5.1, ticked done, requires a throw from canonicalEvent during the walk to be reported as reason hash."}, {"ref": "src/audit/verify.ts:101", "quote": "const computed = chainHash(row.prev_hash, {", "claim": "The walk calls chainHash directly with no try/catch around it, so a throw propagates out of verifyChain."}, {"ref": "src/audit/verify.ts:114", "quote": "if (!prevOk || !computed.equals(row.hash)) {", "claim": "Only a mismatching result is reported as hash; a thrown error is never turned into a report."}, {"ref": "src/audit/hash.ts:43", "quote": "if (!AT_PATTERN.test(rec.at)) {\n    fail(\"bad_at\");", "claim": "canonicalEvent throws AUDIT_EVENT_INVALID bad_at for a stored at text that does not match the pattern, so a walked row can make chainHash throw."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/audit/spec.md#requirement-verifychain-reports-the-first-bad-event", "quote": "each hash equals `chainHash` of the stored row and the head equals the last event; else `{ ok: false, checked, firstBadSeq, reason }` with `reason` `hash` or `gap`", "claim": "The requirement says a row whose stored hash cannot be matched by chainHash yields a report, not a rejection."}]}
